{"translation": "[487] A finer composition will result if one mixes an eighth part of verdigris into the composition made with wax and resin, having first ground the verdigris for several days with the most acrid vinegar. It would be finer still if we were also to mix in frankincense, a half part relative to the verdigris. Of oil you will mix in, when you prepare the drug without vinegar and frankincense, as many cyathi as there are ounces of verdigris. But when you mix in frankincense and vinegar, if the roasted [resin] is somewhat fattier and softer and you are preparing it in summer, you will mix in none; but when it is hard, and in winter, one cyathus. It is also possible for you, if you mix one of the liquid resins with the wax, to need no oil at all. Of the most liquid you will mix in a third of the weight of the wax, and of the less liquid one a half. Such a composition, clearly, will come about as follows: having melted and cooled the wax and the resin, mix them with a part of verdigris, sometimes an eighth, sometimes a tenth, sometimes a twelfth, recognising that for hard bodies the first proportion is suitable, for soft ones the third, and for intermediate ones the intermediate.", "renderings": [{"target_no": 0, "surface": "καλλίων", "english": "finer", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 16, "surface": "ῥητίνης", "english": "resin", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 26, "surface": "δριμυτάτου.", "english": "most acrid", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 74, "surface": "μαλακωτέρα", "english": "softer", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 97, "surface": "ῥητινῶν", "english": "resins", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 113, "surface": "σταθμοῦ,", "english": "weight", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 130, "surface": "ῥητίνην", "english": "resin", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 139, "surface": "ὀγδόῳ,", "english": "an eighth", "uncertain": "n"}], "uncertain_greek": ["ἥμισυ μέρος ἢ κατὰ τὸν ἰόν", "φρυκτὴ"]}
