{"translation": "For earlier I went through only the plasters [728]. But I shall now add those drugs, prepared beforehand in the form of pastilles and mixed with cerates at the time of use, which he says are cicatrizing for ulcers hard to heal, and those that are dry dusting-powders. I begin from the one written in the section on dry drugs near the end. [Dry drugs from those of Andromachus: a dry cicatrizing drug.] Take: burnt bones (otherwise, burnt oyster-shells), 2 dr.; manna, 1 dr.; cadmia, 4 obols (in another copy, 4 dr.). Use finely ground; also for spreading ulcers. Another dry cicatrizing drug. Take: pine bark, 6 dr.; birthwort, 6 dr.; pumice, 4 dr.; dry resin, 4 dr.; manna, 6 dr. It is evident that by this he means the Colophonian resin. Illyrian iris, 2 dr. Use finely ground. Another, which cicatrizes even malignant ulcers. Take: pine bark, 6 dr.; burnt stag's horn, 4 dr.; cadmia, 18 dr.; manna (otherwise, white lead), 4 dr.; scraped verdigris, 2 dr. Use finely ground. Another. Take: oak-gall, 4 dr.; white lead, 8 dr.; myrtle, 4 dr.; litharge, 8 dr.; slag of lead, 4 dr. Use finely ground.", "renderings": [{"target_no": 2, "surface": "ἐμπλάστρους", "english": "plasters", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 13, "surface": "κηρωταῖς", "english": "cerates", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 17, "surface": "ἐπουλωτικά", "english": "cicatrizing", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 53, "surface": "μάννης", "english": "manna", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 56, "surface": "καδμείας", "english": "cadmia", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 72, "surface": "πίτυος", "english": "pine", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 76, "surface": "ἀριστολοχίας", "english": "birthwort", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 93, "surface": "κολοφωνίαν", "english": "Colophonian resin", "uncertain": "n"}], "uncertain_greek": ["μοβύβδου (read as μολύβδου)", "Ὀστέων ἄλλως ὀστρέων", "μάννης, ἄλλως ψιμυθίου", "μιγνυμένων"]}
