{"translation": "In the fourth [787] of these five he goes through the plasters of the same kind as those already written about: some, as Heras has them, identical in every respect; others besides these, which Heras did not mention. These I shall now write out in order, taking care also not to omit any of those written by Heras which he mentions in a different form, as he appears to have done in the case of that of Hicesius. For Crito wrote other weights and measures for this plaster, as did certain others too, not the same as those of Heras. I shall therefore begin with the first, that of Hicesius, since there is disagreement about it concerning the weight of the simple drugs from which they compose the plaster. [The plaster of Hicesius.] Concerning that of Hicesius, Crito wrote word for word as follows.", "renderings": [{"target_no": 8, "surface": "ὁμοειδεῖς", "english": "of the same kind", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 50, "surface": "Ἱκεσίου", "english": "that of Hicesius", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 56, "surface": "σταθμοὺς", "english": "weights", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 60, "surface": "ἐμπλάστρου", "english": "plaster", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 91, "surface": "ἔμπλαστρον.", "english": "plaster", "uncertain": "n"}], "uncertain_greek": ["διαφερόντως", "οὐ τὰς αὐτὰς", "κατὰ πᾶν ὡσαύτως ἐχούσας"]}
