{"translation": "As [853] Ptolemy used it: ℞ burnt lead, orpiment, flake, burnt papyrus, 4 dr. of each; sulphur untouched by fire, 2 dr. Use finely ground. As Apelles used it: a successful drug, entitled 'the one with papyrus', for spreading ulcers. It not only arrests the spreading ulcer but also prevents it when it is beginning. It is also effective for dysenteric patients when infused with rose oil. But when, he says, on being infused in dysenteric patients it produces a biting sensation, the spreading ulcer is to be suspected. The composition is as follows. ℞ burnt papyrus, burnt lead, and burnt and washed copper, orpiment, flake of steel, an equal amount of each; sulphur untouched by fire, half that amount. Use finely ground, either with honey or with rose oil. Moschion's, for spreading ulcers. ℞ elaterium, 2 drachms; burnt papyrus, 2 drachms; copper flake, two drachms; orpiment, 4 drachms; worm verdigris, 1 drachm; ammoniac salt, one drachm. Use finely ground with rose oil. [The fragrant remedy of Lucius the teacher.] ℞ flake, 4 dr.; oak gall, 4 drachms; sandarach, 2 dr.; orpiment, 2 drachms; myrrh, 1 drachm; chalcanthum, 1 drachm.", "renderings": [{"target_no": 8, "surface": "ἀρσενικοῦ,", "english": "orpiment", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 27, "surface": "χάρτου", "english": "papyrus", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 42, "surface": "δυσεντερικοῖς", "english": "dysenteric patients", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 92, "surface": "ἐλατηρίου", "english": "elaterium", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 107, "surface": "σκώληκος", "english": "worm (in 'worm verdigris')", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 111, "surface": "ἀμμωνιακοῦ", "english": "ammoniac", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 117, "surface": "ῥοδίνου.", "english": "rose oil", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 118, "surface": "[Εὐῶδες", "english": "fragrant remedy", "uncertain": "n"}], "uncertain_greek": ["ἀναδάκνηται", "ἐγχυματιζόμενον", "λεπίδος στομώματος", "ἐπιτετευγμένον"]}
